Treat \(V_{DD}\) and both bias voltages as AC ground. Transistor \(M_2\) then presents \(r_{o2}\) from node \(X\) to ground. Since \(M_1\)’s source is at \(X\), this acts as source degeneration when looking into its drain:

\[
\boxed{R_{\text{out}}=r_{o1}+(1+g_{m1}r_{o1})r_{o2}
=r_{o1}+r_{o2}+g_{m1}r_{o1}r_{o2}}
\]

For \(g_{m1}r_{o1}\gg1\), \(R_{\text{out}}\approx g_{m1}r_{o1}r_{o2}\).
